{"case_id":"C015","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","state","input_semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["wuffs_json__decoder.decode_tokens","decoder.decode_digits!"],"reason":"H0 contains only the generic fuzzlib wrapper and declares an external `fuzz(wuffs_base__io_buffer* src, uint32_t hash)`; `fuzz/c/std/json_fuzzer.c` does not exist, and nothing in H0 constructs or invokes a `wuffs_json__decoder`. Consequently, the JSON decoder surface is not exercised, including nested array/object depth up to `decoder_depth_max_incl`, number-length handling in `decoder.decode_digits!`, and the decoder buffer contract represented by `decoder_dst_token_buffer_length_min_incl` and `decoder_src_io_buffer_length_min_incl`. The latter is especially protocol-sensitive because fuzzlib constructs `src.data.len = size`, while S1 specifies that decoder source backing capacity must be at least 100 even when the JSON input itself is shorter.","evidence":["`fuzz/c/std/json_fuzzer.c`: \"This path does not exist in H0.\"","H0 only declares `const char* fuzz(wuffs_base__io_buffer* src, uint32_t hash);` and contains no JSON decoder call.","H0 initializes the input buffer with `.data.len = size`.","S1 defines `WUFFS_JSON__DECODER_SRC_IO_BUFFER_LENGTH_MIN_INCL 100` and explains that this constrains backing-array capacity, not JSON text length.","S1 defines `WUFFS_JSON__DECODER_DST_TOKEN_BUFFER_LENGTH_MIN_INCL 1`.","S1 defines `WUFFS_JSON__DECODER_DEPTH_MAX_INCL 1024`, tied to nested `[]` and `{}` state.","`decoder.decode_digits!` caps supported number length at 99 and explicitly associates that behavior with the 100-byte source-buffer minimum."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated JSON fuzz target implementing `fuzz` that initializes and calls `wuffs_json__decoder`, supplies at least one destination token, uses a source backing array of at least 100 bytes independently of logical input length, and exercises incremental/open-versus-closed input, long numbers